Title: Fix test_archive.sh vacuous test, fixture guard, and test_check.sh live-corpus coupling
Created: 2026-05-05
Author: claude
Closed: done

--- log ---
2026-05-05T08:34Z claude created
2026-05-05T00:00Z claude merged ticket 0010 in

2026-05-05T09:19Z claude closed — done
--- body ---
Three related hygiene issues across two test files.

**1. Vacuous already-archived test in `test_archive.sh` lines ~156-162:**
```sh
OUT4=$($ERG archive "$FIXTURES" 2>&1)
if echo "$OUT4" | grep -q "already exists"; then
    fail "default: already-archived ticket triggers collision (got: $OUT4)"
else
    pass "default: already-archived ticket not re-processed"
```
This passes vacuously: `erg archive` only scans the top-level directory, so
`7001-closed-unblocked.erg` (already in `closed/`) is never examined on the
second pass and never triggers the collision path. The test cannot distinguish
"correctly skipped because already archived" from "silently ignored because the
scanner doesn't look there."

The actual collision-handling path is tested at lines ~165-178 (destination
already exists). Fix: remove the vacuous re-run case and replace it with a
comment explaining why double-archiving is a no-op by design (scanner scope),
or test the property directly — create a ticket, archive it, attempt to archive
by ID a second time, verify nothing changes.

**2. Shared fixture mutation risk in `test_archive.sh`:**
`$FIXTURES/0001-valid.erg` is written once (line ~33) and reused by "multiple
file args pass" and "blocked-by sibling" tests later in the file. Any future
test inserted between creation and reuse that mutates or removes the file will
silently break downstream assertions.

Fix: add an existence assertion immediately before each reuse site:
```sh
[ -f "$FIXTURES/0001-valid.erg" ] || fail "fixture 0001 unexpectedly missing"
```

**3. Live-corpus test in `test_check.sh` at line ~207:**
```sh
$ERG check tickets/   # sanity: live repo must pass erg check
```
This couples CI outcome to editorial decisions in `tickets/`. A legitimately
malformed ticket committed during development would fail CI without any clear
indication that the test suite itself is fine.

Fix: move this assertion to a separate `make validate` target that is
explicitly a lint step, not part of the unit test suite. Add a comment at the
former location explaining where it went.
